      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To investigate the association of thrombospondin-1 (TSP- 1) gene A8831G (N700S) polymorphism with coronary artery disease (CAD)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "This study was conducted with a case-control design including 178 patients with CAD (55 AMI) and 158 healthy subjects. The TSP-1 N700S polymorphism was determined by polymerase chain reaction and restriction fragment length polymorphism analysis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "No significant difference of the AG genotype in CAD group and control group (1.7% compared with 0.6%, P=0.375) was detected. None of the homozygotes was detected for the G allele. The prevalence of the G allele was not significantly different between CAD group and controls (0.8% compared with 0.3%, P=0.376). No significant difference of the AG genotype in AMI group and control group (3.6% compared with 0.6%, P=0.104). The prevalence of G allele was not significantly different between AMI patients and controls (1.8% compared with 0.3%, P=0.364)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "There are TSP-1 N700S polymorphisms in Chinese Zhejiang Han people, but the TSP-1 N700S variant shows a much lower prevalence compared with Western populations and may be not a potential risk for CAD and AMI."
        }
      ]},
